# The app's screens: only these paths serve the app (status 200); every other path that is no file
# gets public/404.html with a 404 status (wrangler.jsonc `not_found_handling`), but /api/* and /ws/*,
# which reach the Worker first (`run_worker_first`) and so have no rule here. The target is `/`, not
# `/index.html`: Cloudflare answers /index.html with a 307 to `/`, which would drop the path.
# apps/web/src/net/deploy-routes.test.ts holds this list to the route table (net/navigate.ts
# `paths`), and cloudflare-serve.test.ts to the pages the build writes.
#
# A page the build writes (apps/web/static-pages.ts) is rewritten to its own folder, not to `/`: a
# rule wins over a file, and a path with no rule gets a 307 to the slashed path. Its slashed path is
# served by the file itself.

